    "description": "Carved Briar Tobacco Pipe\nBent Smoking Pipe With Red Swirl Stem\nBriar Wood & Acrylic, Approximately 5 Inches\nThis vintage estate tobacco smoking pipe features a carved briar bowl in a rounded bent apple profile with a rich reddish-brown finish. Fitted with a silver-tone metal shank band and a curved mouthpiece in marbled red acrylic, it exemplifies mid-to-late 20th century pipe craftsmanship. Carved briar pipes are valued by enthusiasts for their tactile grip and heat dissipation.\nHand-carved scroll and channel texture across the rounded briar bowl\nBent ruby red swirl acrylic stem with silver-tone metal accent band\nStamped numbers 048 and 18 on shank near the band\nMeasures approximately 5 inches in overall length with a 1.9-inch bowl height\nCondition:\nPreviously smoked estate condition. Bowl shows normal carbon cake and rim char from use. Exterior briar carving remains intact with minor surface handling wear. Stem is secure with minor tooth chatter near the lip. Metal collar is firmly seated.",
